Bitmap::allocateHardwareBitmap() must copy source content (host builds)

Upstream: platform/frameworks/base commit 30eb173fa2101eee9f229aff5041712e58f906cf
  "[RNG] Bitmap::allocateHardwareBitmap() must copy source content."
  Author Raphael Moll, 2024-01-24; committed by John Reck, 2025-04-11.
  Change-Id Iddb33172ce95f93f76ebe4733cbbd88a04efefe2, Bug 310222823, 242670053.
  It is the main-branch merge of android12-hostruntime-dev 25874ec and is in
  android-16.0.0_r3 and later, but not in our pin android-16.0.0_r1.
Diff fetched unchanged from
  https://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/base/+/30eb173fa2101eee9f229aff5041712e58f906cf%5E%21/

Why: without it, Bitmap.copy(HARDWARE), HARDWARE decodes (BitmapFactory,
ImageDecoder, BitmapRegionDecoder) and hardware gainmaps return a zeroed
heap bitmap on host. The official Robolectric library (BLR2.250402.052)
copies the pixels: its allocateHardwareBitmap is allocateHeapBitmap(info)
followed by memcpy(dest pixels, src.getPixels(), src.computeByteSize()),
which is the android12-hostruntime-dev form of this change. The two agree
whenever the source has minimal row bytes; readPixels (this commit) also
handles padded rows, where the memcpy form would overrun the destination.

diff --git a/libs/hwui/hwui/Bitmap.cpp b/libs/hwui/hwui/Bitmap.cpp
index 0650169..fbf934e 100644
--- a/libs/hwui/hwui/Bitmap.cpp
+++ b/libs/hwui/hwui/Bitmap.cpp
@@ -212,7 +212,14 @@
 #ifdef __ANDROID__  // Layoutlib does not support hardware acceleration
     return uirenderer::HardwareBitmapUploader::allocateHardwareBitmap(bitmap);
 #else
-    return Bitmap::allocateHeapBitmap(bitmap.info());
+    sk_sp<Bitmap> dest = Bitmap::allocateHeapBitmap(bitmap.info());
+
+    // HardwareBitmapUploader::allocateHardwareBitmap(SkBitmap&) copies Bitmap contents
+    // to a GL texture. To simulate this with an heap bitmap, we use memcpy.
+    auto destPM = dest->getSkBitmap().pixmap();
+    LOG_ALWAYS_FATAL_IF(!bitmap.pixmap().readPixels(destPM), "failed to copy pixels");
+
+    return dest;
 #endif
 }
 
